dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi, carolyn. how are you doing today?
[patient] i'm doing okay. i've just been sitting at the computer a lot lately and i think my osteoarthritis has been flaring up a little bit. i was wondering if we could talk about that. i have a lot of pain in my elbows, but i'm not sure if it's from sitting at the computer or if it's just because i'm getting older.
[doctor] okay. so, let's talk about your osteoarthritis. so you're experiencing pain in your elbows. you said it's been flaring up a little bit. can you tell me more about that?
[patient] yeah, so i just feel like when i sit at the computer, it just feels like my elbows are just kind of stiff and sore. i'm not sure if it's from the computer or if it's just because i'm getting older. i do have a lot of pain in my right elbow versus my left. but i'm not sure if it's because i'm typing all day versus writing. i'm not sure.
[doctor] okay. have you tried doing any exercises or stretches to help with that?
[patient] no, i haven't. i'm not really sure what to do.
[doctor] okay. well, we can talk about some exercises that we can do. but first, let's talk about your gout. how are you doing with your gout?
[patient] i've been doing well. i haven't had any flares since i've been taking the medication.
[doctor] okay. good. we'll continue you on the colchicine 0.6 mg twice a day as needed for flare-ups. but i'm glad to hear you've been doing well with your gout. have you had any issues with your psoriasis?
[patient] no, i have not. i've been doing well.
[doctor] okay. good. we'll continue you on the steroid cream for that. now, let's go ahead and do a physical exam. so i'm going to start with your neck. your neck is supple. i'm not feeling any lymph nodes. let's listen to your lungs. your lungs are clear to auscultation bilaterally. i'm not hearing any wheezes, rales, or rhonchi. let's listen to your heart. your heart is regular rate and rhythm. i'm not hearing any murmurs or gallops. let's listen to your abdomen. your abdomen is soft. i'm not feeling any masses or tenderness. let's go ahead and look at your right elbow. i'm seeing some edema and inflammation of the olecranon. i'm feeling some tenderness to palpation of the olecranon bursa. i'm also feeling pain with pronation and supination. i'm feeling pain with flexion and extension of the right arm. let's go ahead and order an x-ray of your right elbow. i'm going to prescribe meloxicam 15 mg once a day for your pain and swelling. i'm also going to continue you on the colchicine for your gout. and we'll continue you on the steroid cream for your psoriasis. i'm going to send you home with a prescription for meloxicam. you can start taking it as needed. and i'm going to order that x-ray of your right elbow. and we'll go ahead and schedule that for today. are you okay with that?
[patient] yes, i'm okay with that.
[doctor] okay. well, i'll go ahead and go ahead and order that x-ray and we'll go ahead and schedule that for today. and then i'll go ahead and prescribe the meloxicam for you. and we'll go ahead and continue you on the colchicine and the steroid cream. are you okay with all of that?
[patient] yes, i'm okay with that. }}<|eot_id|>
