dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hey jordan how are you doing today
[patient] i'm doing good
[doctor] good good hey i'm dr johnson and i'm your primary care physician here at the medical group and i'm happy to be seeing you today so what brings you in today
[patient] i'm having a lot of palpitations
[doctor] okay okay and i understand that you've had some palpitations in the past and you've had some high blood pressure and you've been monitoring your blood pressure at home and you've been noticing that your blood pressure's been running a little bit higher than usual
[patient] yeah i've been having palpitations and i've been having high blood pressure and i've been monitoring it and i've been trying to cut back on the salt and i've been walking on the treadmill every day
[doctor] okay okay good good good okay so let's talk a little bit more about your palpitations so when you were in the emergency room in march you went in for palpitations and you said that you had a panic attack and you had consumed a lot of coffee on an empty stomach that morning and you said that you had not had any other episodes of palpitations since then
[patient] that's correct
[doctor] okay okay and you've been doing okay with your blood pressure since then
[patient] yeah i've been doing good
[doctor] okay okay good good good so i'm going to review your chart here real quick okay so i see that you've been on benicar hct for a little while now how's that going
[patient] it's going good
[doctor] okay good good good and i'm going to go ahead and order a thyroid profile here today
[patient] okay
[doctor] and i'm going to order a basic metabolic panel as well so i can get a look at your electrolytes and your kidney function okay good good so i'm going to go ahead and review your blood pressure here real quick and i see that your blood pressure's been running a little bit high so i'm going to go ahead and review your physical exam okay so i'm going to go ahead and listen to your heart and your heart sounds are normal your heart rate is regular your blood pressure is a little bit elevated but it's not alarmingly high but i do want to talk to you about your blood pressure and we need to work on getting that under control okay so i'm going to go ahead and review your medications real quick and i see that you're on amlodipine and benicar hct so let's talk about your medications okay so i'm going to go ahead and add spironolactone to your regimen which is a diuretic that will help with your blood pressure and we'll also add some potassium and sodium monitoring to that and we'll follow up in two weeks to check your blood pressure and we'll also do a basic metabolic panel and i'll be able to check your potassium and sodium levels and if we're not able to get your blood pressure under control with spironolactone then we'll need to consider adding carvedilol which is a beta blocker which can help with your heart rate and your blood pressure and i'm going to go ahead and counsel you on some of the side effects of spironolactone so we'll talk about some of the potential side effects of gynecomastia and some electrolyte disturbances and some of the signs to watch for are dizziness and if we're not able to get your blood pressure under control with the spironolactone then we'll need to consider sending you to the resistant hypertension clinic and i'll go ahead and review some materials with you on the american heart association website heart.org and i encourage you to access that website and look at some of the tips on lowering your salt intake and increasing your potassium intake and i'm going to encourage you to try to reduce your sodium intake to 1500 to 2000 milligrams per day and i'll also encourage you to follow the dash diet and i'll provide you with some materials on that and i encourage you to try to walk at least 30 minutes most days
[patient] okay
[doctor] and we'll schedule a follow up appointment in two weeks to check your blood pressure and we'll do a basic metabolic panel and we'll see how you're doing okay good good good so any questions for me today
[patient] no i think that's it
[doctor] okay okay good good good all right so we'll go ahead and schedule that appointment for two weeks from today and i'll see you then
[patient] okay
[doctor] and i'll also give you a prescription for spironolactone and we'll go ahead and get you started on that and we'll go ahead and get you set up with a basic metabolic panel and we'll go ahead and get that ordered and we'll go ahead and get that scheduled for the next two weeks and i'll see you then
[patient] okay
[doctor] okay good good good
[patient] thank you
[doctor] okay you're welcome
[patient] thank you
[doctor] okay
[patient] bye
[doctor] bye }}<|eot_id|>
