dialogue is: {{ [doctor] good morning, brittany. how are you doing today?
[patient] i'm doing well, doctor. i'm feeling a little bit better.
[doctor] good. i'm glad to hear that. so, i understand you're here today to follow up on your irritable bowel syndrome. how's that been going?
[patient] i've been doing alright. i've been having some flare ups. i've been having some cramps and sharp pains, but i think i've been doing a little better.
[doctor] okay. good. what have you been doing to manage those symptoms?
[patient] i've been taking my bentyl and i've been taking my probiotics. i've been eating a little better. i've been trying to eat more fiber. i've been eating more fruits and vegetables. i've been doing a little better.
[doctor] okay. that's great. i'm glad to hear that. have you been eating any foods that you know trigger your symptoms?
[patient] well, i had shrimp yesterday and i had some upper and lower abdominal pain and some bloating. but i think it was just because i ate the shrimp. i had chicken alfredo and had diarrhea. but i don't think the alfredo contributed to my symptoms.
[doctor] okay. so the shrimp was the culprit there?
[patient] yeah.
[doctor] okay. and how much do you drink when you're out?
[patient] i have 2 drinks. i have either tequila or brown liquor. i have a martini every now and then. i try to avoid heavy foods, but i had fried chicken today. and i've stopped drinking soda. that's been really helpful.
[doctor] okay. that's great. you're doing a good job with that. and have you noticed any changes in your bowel movements?
[patient] yeah. i've been having diarrhea every now and then. i've been passing 2 to 3 formed stools a day.
[doctor] okay. well, let's go ahead and take a look at you. i'm going to listen to your heart and lungs. and i'm going to listen to your abdomen. i'm not hearing any abnormal heart sounds. your lungs are clear. and your abdomen is soft and non-tender. you don't have any masses or organomegaly. your bowel sounds are normoactive.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. so, let's talk about your symptoms. how would you rate your nausea? would you say it's a 1, 2, 3, 4, or 5?
[patient] i would say a 2.
[doctor] okay. and how would you rate your abdominal pain? would you say it's a 1, 2, 3, 4, or 5?
[patient] i would say a 3.
[doctor] okay. and how would you rate your diarrhea? would you say it's a 1, 2, 3, 4, or 5?
[patient] i would say a 2.
