dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hey, so, um, i'm dr. katz. i'm a doctor here at the clinic. i'm here to see you today, um, for some full-spectrum std testing. how are you doing today? }} {{ [patient] i'm doing okay. i'm a little nervous, but i'm fine. }} {{ [doctor] okay, well, um, let's start with your history. what brings you in today? }} {{ [patient] i'm having symptoms of discomfort, um, a change in discharge, and an odor in my vaginal region. i'm having a little bit of pain on the right side of my vagina. i'm not really having any fever or chills. but i did find out that my partner of three years has been having sex with other people, so i'm worried that i might have gotten something from them. }} {{ [doctor] okay. okay, um, so, um, let's start with the pain. where is the pain located? is it just on the right side, or is it on both sides? }} {{ [patient] it's just on the right side. }} {{ [doctor] okay. and is the pain constant or does it come and go? }} {{ [patient] it's kind of constant, but it's not really painful. it's just a little uncomfortable. }} {{ [doctor] okay. um, and have you noticed any changes in your discharge? has it changed in color or smell or consistency? }} {{ [patient] yeah, i've noticed a change in the odor and the color and the consistency of my discharge. it's been a little bit more yellowish and it smells really bad. and the consistency is a little bit thicker than it used to be. }} {{ [doctor] okay. okay, um, have you noticed any pain with urination? }} {{ [patient] no, i'm not having any pain with urination. }} {{ [doctor] okay, um, have you had any fever or chills? }} {{ [patient] no, i'm not having any fever or chills. }} {{ [doctor] okay, um, okay. so, um, let's talk a little bit about your sexual history. how many sexual partners have you had in the last six months? }} {{ [patient] i've had one. }} {{ [doctor] okay, okay. and how about in the last year? }} {{ [patient] um, i've had one. }} {{ [doctor] okay. okay, um, and how about in your lifetime? }} {{ [patient] i've had two. }} {{ [doctor] okay. okay, um, are you using condoms? }} {{ [patient] um, sometimes. i try to. }} {{ [doctor] okay. okay, um, and have you had any abnormal pap smears in the past? }} {{ [patient] yeah, i had an abnormal pap smear when i was 20. but all my pap smears since then, including my most recent one about six months ago, have all been normal. }} {{ [doctor] okay. okay, um, okay. let's go ahead and do a physical exam. let's take a look at your abdomen. everything looks normal. let's take a look at your genitalia. everything looks normal. um, let's take a look at your cervix. everything looks normal. um, i'm going to go ahead and do a pelvic exam. i'm going to go ahead and do a pap smear. everything looks normal. i'm going to go ahead and do a rectal exam. everything looks normal. i'm going to go ahead and do a breast exam. everything looks normal. i'm going to go ahead and do a general physical exam. everything looks normal. i'm going to go ahead and do a neuro exam. everything looks normal. i'm going to go ahead and do a cardiovascular exam. everything looks normal. i'm going to go ahead and do a respiratory exam. everything looks normal. i'm going to go ahead and do an abdominal exam. everything looks normal. let's go ahead and get the results of the pap smear. and i'm going to go ahead and order a full-spectrum std test. so we're going to test for gonorrhea, chlamydia, trichomoniasis, syphilis, hiv, and hepatitis c. and i'm going to go ahead and call you with the results. so, um, let's go ahead and get you set up for the std test. let's go ahead and get you set up for the pap smear. and let's go ahead and get you set up for the pelvic exam. and let's go ahead and get you set up for the breast exam. and let's go ahead and get you set up for the abdominal exam. and let's go ahead and get you set up for the neuro exam. and let's go ahead and get you set up for the cardiovascular exam. and let's go ahead and get you set up for the respiratory exam. so, um, i'm going to go ahead and go ahead and order all of the necessary tests. and i'm going to go ahead and call you with the results. so, um, let's go ahead and get you set up for the std test. and let's go ahead and get you set up for the pap smear. and let's go ahead and get you set up for the pelvic exam. and let's go ahead and get you set up for the breast exam. and let's go ahead and get you set up for the abdominal exam. and let's go ahead and get you set up for the neuro exam. and let's go ahead and get you set up for the cardiovascular exam. and let's go ahead and get you set up for the respiratory exam. }} {{ [patient] okay. }} {{ [doctor] okay. }} {{ [patient] um, thanks. }} {{ [doctor] okay. }} }}<|eot_id|>
