dialogue is: {{ [doctor] jacqueline miller is a 40-year-old female who is being seen today for a follow-up skin exam for perioral dermatitis. she also has a history of rosacea, including ocular rosacea. how are you today?

[jacqueline] i'm doing okay.

[doctor] good. so let's talk about your perioral dermatitis. how has it been going?

[jacqueline] it's doing well. i've been using the doxycycline and it's been helping. i've just been using it once a day since the pharmacist told me to.

[doctor] okay. so the pharmacist advised you to reduce the frequency of the doxycycline. how's that been working?

[jacqueline] it's been okay. i haven't seen a lot of improvement. it's not gotten worse, but it's not gotten better either.

[doctor] okay. have you been using the sulfacetamide wash as directed?

[jacqueline] yes, twice a day.

[doctor] and have you been using the metrocream after washing your face?

[jacqueline] yes, i have.

[doctor] good. have you been using any other lotions, creams, or products on your skin?

[jacqueline] no, i've been trying to avoid that.

[doctor] okay. and have you started the elidel yet?

[jacqueline] no, i haven't started it because it's not covered by my insurance and i'm concerned about the side effects.

[doctor] okay. well, let's take a look at your skin. so your skin looks good. i do see a few very faint erythematous papules on the medial cheeks, and some mild redness around and underneath the nostrils. your skin type is a four to five. let's talk about your rosacea. how's that been going?

[jacqueline] it's been okay. it's been a little bit worse lately.

[doctor] okay. so you've had some flares of rosacea. have you been using the metrocream as directed?

[jacqueline] yes, i have.

[doctor] good. and have you been washing your eyelids gently with a gentle cleanser?

[jacqueline] yes, i have.

[doctor] okay. have you tried any other creams or ointments on your eyelids?

[jacqueline] no, i've been trying to avoid that.

[doctor] okay. well, i'm going to prescribe you some tacrolimus cream. it's a topical steroid that should help with the redness and itching of the rosacea. i'm also going to prescribe you some vanicream. it's a gentle cream that you can use on your eyelids to help with the rosacea. i want you to gently wash your eyelids with a gentle cleanser once a day and then apply the vanicream. i want you to continue using the metrocream twice a day on your face. i want you to continue using the sulfacetamide wash once a day. i also want you to use a bruder mask as needed. i want you to continue the doxycycline twice a day until you've reached full resolution of the perioral dermatitis, and then you can reduce it to once a day for an additional week. i want you to call the clinic if your symptoms worsen. you'll have a follow-up appointment in four weeks. is that okay?

[jacqueline] that sounds good. }}<|eot_id|>
