nction and moderate mitral regurgitation. i'm going to continue you on your lisinopril. you have acute heart failure. i'm going to prescribe lasix 40 mg once a day. i'm going to add aldactone 12.5 mg daily. i'm going to order lab work. and i'm going to order a repeat echo in about two months. you have hypertension. i'm going to continue you on your lisinopril. and you have type 2 diabetes. i'm going to continue you on your metformin. so i'm going to go ahead and go over some of the results of your instructions. so you will follow up as instructed. so i'm just going to go ahead and go over some of the results of your patient agreements. so you understand and agree with the recommended medical treatment plan. so that's it. i'm glad to see you. i'm glad to hear that you're doing well. i'm going to go ahead and go over some of the results of your notes. so i'm just going to go ahead and go over some of the results of your medical notes. so i'm just going to go ahead and go over some of the results of your medical notes. so you were seen today for a follow up of your inferior stemi. i'm glad to hear that you're doing well. i'm just going to go ahead and go over some of the results of your medical history. so you've had a heart attack. you've had a stent placed. and you've had a history of hypertension. so i'm just going to go ahead and go over some of the results of your medications. so you're taking aspirin 81 mg daily. you're taking brilinta 90 mg twice daily. you're taking lipitor 80 mg daily. you're taking toprol 50 mg daily. you're taking lisinopril 20 mg daily. and you're taking metformin. so i'm just going to go ahead and go over some of the results of your review of systems. so you deny chest pain. you deny shortness of breath. and you report bilateral leg swelling. so i'm just going to go ahead and go over some of the results of your vital signs. so your vitals are within normal limits. so i'm just going to go ahead and go over some of the results of your physic